@startuml
!include common.iuml
start
:Load IrrigationAdvisoryDataset.csv (1,000 plots);
:Impute missing NDVI with village median;
:Drop constant columns (area, district, sampling);
:Augment: 12 seasonal scenarios per plot\n(crop age, heat, dry spell, rain forecast);
:Label with agronomy engine\n(FAO-56 water balance, FAO-33 yield response);
:Add field-realistic label noise;
:GroupShuffleSplit by plot (80% train / 20% test);
fork
  :Train RF regressor\n(next irrigation);
fork again
  :Train GBM regressors\n(ETc, depth, yield);
fork again
  :Train RF classifiers\n(water stress, disease risk);
fork again
  :Build delay-augmented set\nand train GBM (yield loss);
end fork
:Evaluate on unseen plots\nvs linear / logistic baselines;
:K-Means (k=4) management zones on real plots;
:Export trees and zones to JSON;
:Write metrics.json and test fixtures;
if (Node parity tests pass?) then (yes)
  :Serve models from Node.js API;
else (no)
  :Investigate export / feature order;
endif
stop
@enduml
